@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] personal-sheet-shares-owned-native-flow
Android and iOS MUST render the same personal account sheet and consume the shared
source-owned sign-in/account runtime. The native host MUST use the system browser and
report its actual foreground lifecycle synchronously through the runtime port, before
any deferred UI update; browser background MUST pause polling without
discarding the in-memory attempt. Closing the sheet or retiring its entry MUST close
the controller and release pending recovery ownership synchronously before the host's
close callback, rather than waiting for composition disposal. Only a securely staged, server-
confirmed and atomically promoted session MAY appear as connected. GitHub/provider
tokens MUST NOT reach this UI. Errors MUST use fixed localized recovery, and an absent
configured capability MUST remain unavailable without blocking anonymous browsing.
Personal promotion/sign-out MUST revoke the prior public source and reset the same
navigation stack to Explore, without adopting legacy private authority. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 any-GitHub/public-browsing request, maximum-reuse iOS decision and accepted
22 Oct native secure-stage/confirm/publish protocol and independent mounted-account
ownership review.
